# decision tools.deps git coordinates stay commit-pinned

The Clojure adapter owns one delimited qualified lib entry in the top-level `:deps` map in
`deps.edn`. It writes `:git/url` and the full lock commit as `:git/sha`; `:deps/root` carries an
export subdirectory. tools.deps is always pinned to `LockedDependency.Commit`.
When the root map has no `:deps`, the adapter creates a delimited top-level `:deps` entry and
removes that entire entry on unwire. Inline closing braces use a distinct delimiter so insertion
and removal do not manufacture a newline.

# test Clojure adapter

- Fixture/golden wiring is idempotent and preserves unrelated EDN forms and comments.
- Unqualified library names are typed not-wirable.
- Drift checks the normalized Git URL and full SHA; unwire removes only the delimited entry.

# decision tools.deps materialization

`Capability` rejects an unqualified lib symbol before mutation. `Pull` and `Remove` require the
`clj` tools.deps command before editing and run `clj -P` afterwards, so the current dependency set
is prepared without evaluating consumer code. `Inspect` remains offline and verifies the exact
commit checkout in tools.deps `.gitlibs`; it checks the JVM account home and `HOME` because those
may differ, without invoking `clj` for discovery.

The pinned adapter-local Docker test drives init/add/list/pull/remove through the public CLI and
proves actual namespace loading, read-only missing-checkout reporting, same-commit repair,
fresh-clone materialization, branch advancement, idempotence, and preservation of an unrelated lib.
